## Phase scope

Make every fs root and bound port honor environment variables. Process-level multi-tenancy depends on it.

**Tasks:**
- [ ] Create `getDataRoot()` utility. Likely lives in `packages/shared/paths/` (new) or an existing `@slayzone/shared` package — check first.
- [ ] Replace ~12 sites of `process.env.SLAYZONE_DB_DIR || app.getPath('userData')` with `getDataRoot()`.
- [ ] Fix hardcoded `Extensions/` and `browser-extensions.json` paths (browser domain).
- [ ] Audit `app.getPath()` call sites. Electron-only packages may keep them; any code destined for the server package must not depend on Electron.
- [ ] Confirm `SLAYZONE_PORT`, `SLAYZONE_MCP_PORT` honored at every bind site. Add `SLAYZONE_HOST` (default `localhost`).
- [ ] Smoke test: run two `pnpm dev` instances side-by-side with different `SLAYZONE_DB_DIR` + `SLAYZONE_PORT`. Verify zero data crossover.

**Done criteria:** can spin up two isolated dev instances on one machine.

