**Smoke-test approach:**
- Script spawns two `pnpm dev` w/ distinct `SLAYZONE_DB_DIR=/tmp/slay-a` + `/tmp/slay-b`, distinct `SLAYZONE_MCP_PORT=4848` + `4849`.
- After 30s warmup: assert `/tmp/slay-a/slayzone.dev.sqlite` exists, `/tmp/slay-b/slayzone.dev.sqlite` exists, sizes independent (touch one DB via CLI → other unchanged).
- Assert ports bound: `lsof -iTCP:4848` + `lsof -iTCP:4849` both return Electron PIDs.
- Assert Extensions dirs separate: `ls /tmp/slay-{a,b}/Extensions/`.
- Cleanup: kill both PIDs.
- Single-instance lock concern: see Open Questions #1 below — likely need to gate `requestSingleInstanceLock()` when `SLAYZONE_DB_DIR` is set, otherwise smoke test cannot run two instances at all.

